Spec: TenantMod

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  Sub-command dispatcher for `agent tenant …`: owns the private `backup`, `delete`,
    `install`, `restore` modules (and the commented-out `reconfigure`), exposes one clap
    group and one async entry initializing the Kubernetes client before dispatch. The
    file is byte-identical to ./../service/mod.rs (diff-verified; frozen in
    ./../service/mod.sdd) — type differences live only in the leaves.

Owns:
  ./mod.rs

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap `Parser`, `Debug`; single field @command: @Commands. Consumed by
    ./../main.rs (`Tenant` dispatch arm; spec pending ./../main.sdd).
  @Commands — clap `Subcommand`, `Debug`, four live variants:
    @Install(install::Parameters), @Delete(delete::Parameters),
    @Backup(backup::Parameters), @Restore(restore::Parameters).
  @run — async, takes `&Parameters`, returns `()`.

Accepts:
  A parsed @Commands tree; every flag contract lives in the leaf specs.

Returns:
  `()` — success falls off the end, each @Err lane ends in @std::process::exit.

Handles:
  Leaf @Err per arm: Install `Installing a package failed with: {e:}` → exit 1;
    Delete `Deleting a package failed with: {e:}` → exit 3;
    Backup `Backup of a package failed with: {e:}` → exit 4;
    Restore `Restore of a package failed with: {e:}` → exit 5.
  Panics inside leaves — unwound to main's runtime.

Must:
  Keep `mod backup; mod delete; mod install; mod restore;` private and
    `//mod reconfigure;` commented (./reconfigure.sdd is out of the build graph).
  Keep the commented @Reconfigure variant and exit-6 arm commented in lockstep.
  Call @common::context::init_k8s() once before the match.
  Await @install::run/@delete::run; call @backup::run/@restore::run synchronously.
  Carry the same `//`-comment help quirk on @Backup/@Restore as the service twin.

Depends on:
  ./install.sdd, ./delete.sdd, ./backup.sdd, ./restore.sdd, ./reconfigure.sdd (dead
    sibling) — tenant leaf contracts.
  ./../service/mod.sdd — the byte-identical twin; keep both in lockstep on any change.
  ../common/src/context.sdd — @init_k8s.
  ./../main.rs — caller; spec pending ./../main.sdd.

Tasks:
  [ ] Decide later whether the byte-identical service/tenant dispatcher pair should be
      one generic module or stay hand-copied.
  [ ] Decide the fate of the commented Reconfigure lane (shared with service).
  [ ] Cover this dispatcher with tests; none exist.

Done when:
  Dispatch, init ordering, exit ladder, and the twin-frozen identity hold under tests.

Scenario: tenant delete failure exits 3
  Given `TenantMod` @Commands::Delete whose leaf returns @Err
  When @run reaches the Delete arm
  Then the frozen delete log line prints and @process::exit(3) is reached

Scenario: install runs after cluster init
  Given @Commands::Install with valid leaf flags
  When @run is awaited
  Then @common::context::init_k8s precedes @install::run (./install.sdd) and @Ok ends
    @run with no exit call
